            "review_title": "Review at Sanuki Udon-135 Nguyễn Văn Linh",
            "review_text": "Mashajo\nKaliningrad, Russia11593 contributions\n28\nJapanese noodles\nJul 2025 • Solo\nI was nearby and I saw this place, I thought I'd come in for dinner. It's a small cafe specializing in Japanese noodles. The interior is pleasant and cozy: on the walls of a painting with Japanese motifs, the ceiling is decorated with flashlights - atmospheric. The employees are friendly. English is hardly used, but it's not an inconvenience at all - it's clear and without words. There is a wide selection of Japanese cuisine on the menu, no alcohol. Prices are pleasant, payment by card accepted without additional %. I ordered oudon noodles with beef. Brought in quickly. The portion is large, the meat and vegetables are sufficient, the broth is rich and very delicious. The service is attentive. It's a good place to have a quiet dinner.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten December 9, 2025",
